There is no single universally accepted answer.\line Most people in everyday life treat it as }{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\cs16\rtlch\ab \ltrch\loch\b\fs22\b0\loch
the same ship}{\rtlch\afs22\ab0 \ltrch\loch\fs22\b0\loch
 (because continuity of structure and history matters more to us than the original atoms). Strictly speaking, however, the paradox shows that our ordinary concept of \uc2 \u8220\'81\'67sameness\u8221\'81\'68 over time is more complicated \u8212\'81\'5c and less precise \u8212\'81\'5c than it first appears.\uc1 }
